# .canaryignore - Gitignore-style patterns for CANARY token scanning
#
# This file specifies files and directories that should be ignored when
# scanning for CANARY tokens. Patterns follow gitignore syntax.
#
# Common patterns:
# - Use # for comments
# - Use / for directory separators
# - Use * for wildcards
# - Use ** for recursive wildcards
# - Use ! to negate patterns (whitelist)
# - Patterns are relative to the root directory

# Template and AI agent configuration directories
.canary/
.claude/
.cursor/
.github/
.windsurf/
.kilocode/
.roo/
.opencode/
.codex/
.augment/
.codebuddy/
.amazonq/

# Documentation directories (often contain example tokens)
# Anchored to root only (CP-285): a bare "docs/"/"specs/" matches ANY
# directory with that name at any depth under gitignore semantics, which
# would silently exclude nested dirs like pkg/docs/ or pkg/specs/ from
# scans/upgrades in projects generated from this template.
/docs/
/specs/

# Build artifacts
bin/
dist/
build/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Dependencies and caches
node_modules/
vendor/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.cache/

# Test data (may contain fixture tokens)
testdata/
fixtures/
test-fixtures/
*_test.go

# Version control
.git/
.direnv/

# Backups written by `canary init --force` and `canary upgrade --write`.
# One generation deep: <file>.bak holds the bytes replaced by the most recent
# rewrite of that file and is overwritten by the next one. The scanner skips
# them by default too, so a stale token inside a .bak never counts.
*.bak

# Generated files
status.json
status.csv
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# IDE files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
